      <section id="faq" class="section_libraries-faq">
        <div class="page-padding-5 max">
          <div class="container-large-5">
            <h2 class="heading-sections left">Frequently asked questions<br></h2>
            <div class="w-layout-hflex flex-block-30">
              <div class="faq-sub left-sub">Product &amp; Capabilities<br></div>
              <div class="libraries-faq_component">
                <div class="libraries-faq_expand-wrapper">
                  <div class="w-layout-grid libraries-faq_layout">
                    <ul role="list" class="w-layout-grid libraries-faq_list top wf-semantic-list">
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion _1st">
                        <div data-w-id="0d1291ff-098a-8124-6f72-ce301126971f" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">What is Olostep?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Olostep is <strong>Web Infrastructure for Knowledge work AIs</strong>. It started by providing a suite of Web Data APIs that let businesses’ AI agents search, extract, and structure web data. It helps AI application companies turn public web content into clean, structured outputs. Olostep&#x27;s mission is to make the world&#x27;s data useful to knowledge work AIs and become the business operating systems of AI-native companies.</p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="ec2aa77e-12b0-2f4d-4b21-8364b1de77a1" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">Why are we building Olostep?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Olostep is built on a bet that, over time, most knowledge work will flow through AI models. A new generation of AI application companies is emerging to assist and automate knowledge work in specific domains, such as marketing, manufacturing, legal and property appraisals. Olostep exists for them: the data infrastructure for their agents, enterprise-ready and embedded in their core products.<br><br>Those agents are shifting from writing text to making decisions. Decision models return a choice with a probability that code can act on directly, imbuing software itself with intelligence. Every decision needs fresh, domain-specific data and produces new data in turn. Within a year, these companies will rebuild around decision loops and lock in the infrastructure underneath. Olostep is positioned to be that infrastructure.</p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="2c93b9a6-cbad-a21a-257e-0f190dd8d492" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">Why do AI agents need web infrastructure?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">The primary users of the web are shifting from humans to AI agents. Today, billions of people use the web. Tomorrow,<strong> trillions of agents will use it</strong><br><br>These agents need web infrastructure built specifically for them — infrastructure that can help them access information, assist people, and automate knowledge work at a scale the web has never seen before.</p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="3d2c2534-56cc-9836-d90d-d7cc7f8ae91c" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">How is Olostep different?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Olostep is an <strong>infrastructure company for knowledge-work AIs, where data is a first-class citizen</strong>: data as infrastructure.<br><br>We’re not building Google for agents (search-as-infrastructure) or a developer tool. Search APIs index the whole web for anyone; we index the portions that matter to our customers and capture snapshots over time, so their agents see not just what the web says but what changed. And we’re built for AI knowledge-work businesses and their teams, not individual developers: enterprise-ready and embedded in their core products. <br><br>Our mission is to make the world’s data useful to knowledge-work AIs and to become the business operating system of AI-native companies.</p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="0d1291ff-098a-8124-6f72-ce3011269747" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">Why should I use Olostep?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Olostep is built for business use cases: reliable, scalable, cost-effective, flexible and designed to fit your existing workflows and backend. It’s enterprise-ready, trusted by teams that run it inside their core products. You can build custom parsers that return deterministic, structured results at scale, so your agents and decision models always get data in the exact shape they need. And our talent-dense team works alongside yours, building the features your product needs. You can test Olostep for free to see if it fits your use case. Get your free API keys <a href="https://www.olostep.com/auth/"><span class="text-span-209"><em class="italic-text-3">here</em></span></a><span><em>.</em></span><br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="8ca1398e-8ce7-a2bc-abcf-fcc2389aa148" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">Who should use Olostep?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Olostep is built for AI agents deployed within businesses, especially agents built by AI application companies that assist areas of knowledge work — from AI for marketers and engineers to AI for lawyers and property appraisals.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                          <div data-w-id="ab199d1b-4eee-64bc-81c6-13be3192c904" class="libraries-faq_question">
                            <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">What is a Web Data API?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                          </div>
                          <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                            <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                              <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">A Web Data API allows developers to extract, crawl and structure data from websites at scale. It handles rendering, anti-bot protection and parsing, returning clean outputs such as JSON or HTML for use in applications, analytics or AI workflows.</p>
                            </div>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="0d1291ff-098a-8124-6f72-ce3011269729" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">Can Olostep support my high-volume requests?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Yes, Olostep is built to handle high-volume data extraction at scale, supporting up to billions of requests per month. With features like batch processing, distributed infrastructure and scalable workflows, it is designed for both growing teams and enterprise-level use cases.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="w-layout-hflex flex-block-30">
              <div class="faq-sub left-sub">Usage &amp; Automation<br></div>
              <div class="libraries-faq_component">
                <div class="libraries-faq_expand-wrapper">
                  <div class="w-layout-grid libraries-faq_layout">
                    <ul role="list" class="w-layout-grid libraries-faq_list top wf-semantic-list">
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion _1st">
                        <div data-w-id="bc48a488-a1d5-b7ac-ada6-2d3df5f039c1" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">How does a Web Data API work?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">A Web Data API processes requests by rendering web pages, handling anti-bot protections, extracting structured data and returning it in formats such as JSON or Markdown. This removes the need to manage scraping infrastructure manually.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="9e973d62-7170-7a7c-e362-91c47e7fab11" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">What is the difference between crawling and scraping?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Crawling refers to discovering and navigating multiple pages across a website, while scraping focuses on extracting data from a specific page. A Web Data API typically supports both processes in a unified workflow.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="bc48a488-a1d5-b7ac-ada6-2d3df5f039cb" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">What formats does Olostep return results in?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Most Web Data APIs return data in structured formats such as JSON, as well as HTML, Markdown or raw content depending on the use case. Structured outputs are commonly used for automation and AI workflows.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="bc48a488-a1d5-b7ac-ada6-2d3df5f039df" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">Can Olostep automate my data pipelines?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Yes, Olostep is designed to support automated data pipelines and research workflows on the web. With capabilities for searching, crawling, scraping, structuring data and running repeatable workflows, it can support a wide range of business and AI use cases.<br>‍<br>If you have a specific workflow in mind, contact the team at info@olostep.com or via the Contact Sales page to discuss the best setup for your use case.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="bc48a488-a1d5-b7ac-ada6-2d3df5f0395c" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">Can I extract data with a prompt?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Yes, Olostep lets you extract data using natural language prompts. If you already know the exact page you want to process, you can use the <code>/scrapes</code> endpoint with LLM extraction to describe the data you want returned.<br><br>For high-volume or deterministic extraction, Olostep&#x27;s parsers are the better option, as they return structured JSON more consistently at scale.<br><br>For more advanced workflows, such as searching for data, navigating across pages, handling pagination or validating results, the <code>/agents</code> endpoint can automatically carry out multi-step extraction based on your prompt.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="bc48a488-a1d5-b7ac-ada6-2d3df5f03966" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">What is counted as a request?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">One request equals one webpage or one PDF processed. We do not charge separately for bandwidth, proxies, or data usage. All infrastructure costs are included in the price per request.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="67ace6a0-7b76-7639-7c6c-4c32109bc717" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">Does Olostep charge for failed requests?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">No, Olostep does not charge for failed requests. You are only billed for successful requests, ensuring predictable and fair usage-based pricing.<br><br>For endpoints that involve LLM processing (such as the Answers API), any underlying model costs may still apply. However, Olostep itself only charges for requests that are successfully completed.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion"></li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="w-layout-hflex flex-block-30">
              <div class="faq-sub left-sub">Pricing &amp; Plans<br></div>
              <div class="libraries-faq_component">
                <div class="libraries-faq_expand-wrapper">
                  <div class="w-layout-grid libraries-faq_layout">
                    <ul role="list" class="w-layout-grid libraries-faq_list wf-semantic-list">
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion _1st">
                        <div data-w-id="4781fdc4-d17f-e1ee-55ee-4696a8b9a690" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">Does Olostep offer a free trial?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Yes, Olostep includes a free plan with 500 requests to help you test the API before upgrading. Paid plans start from $9/month and include 5,000 credits per month.<br><br>This gives teams a low-risk way to evaluate Olostep&#x27;s reliability, scalability and cost-effectiveness before moving to higher-volume usage.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="4781fdc4-d17f-e1ee-55ee-4696a8b9a6ac" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">Can I switch plans after signing up?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Yes, you can switch plans at any time. Plans are pro-rated, meaning any unused value from your current plan is carried over to your new plan.<br><br>This ensures you don&#x27;t pay twice for usage you&#x27;ve already covered, giving you flexibility as your needs grow.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="4781fdc4-d17f-e1ee-55ee-4696a8b9a6b6" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">Can I ask for a refund if I don&#x27;t use it?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">Yes. If you&#x27;re not satisfied with the Olostep API or it doesn&#x27;t end up being useful for your use case, you can email <a href="mailto:info@olostep.com?subject=I&#x27;d%20like%20a%20refund">info@olostep.com</a> to request a refund.<br><br>If you cancel after a period of non-use, Olostep can also refund the unused portion of your plan where applicable.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                      <li class="libraries-faq_accordion">
                        <div data-w-id="4781fdc4-d17f-e1ee-55ee-4696a8b9a6c0" class="libraries-faq_question">
                          <h3 class="text-size-large-2 text-weight-medium">How can I pay?</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/6177739448baa6e16cce1db4_icon_plus.svg" alt="" class="libraries-faq_icon">
                        </div>
                        <div style="height:0px" class="libraries-faq_answer">
                          <div class="margin-bottom margin-small">
                            <p class="text-color-grey text-size-medium">You can pay through Stripe Payment Links. To access billing, you must be logged in to your Olostep account. Go to your dashboard, navigate to Billing &amp; Invoices, click Manage on Stripe, and add your card details. Once your card is added, you’re good to go.<br></p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="section-centered image">
        <div class="container-sections">
          <div class="body-head-sub">
            <h2 class="quote">Making the world&#x27;s data useful to AIs doing knowledge work</h2>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
